e second reason I'd recommend buying  one of these is the fact that it's a  hands-free calculator now no that's a  bit of a weird one to bring up in a top  five video but for my situation is  something that I use quite a lot if I'm  sitting on my laptop doing some econ  work I can easily just go what's ten  plus ten or  what's fifty seven times thirty-two and  it's gonna give me an answer straight  away the third reason to buy one of  these little devices is the fact that  it's super helpful and convenient with  now if you're somebody like me that's  always thinking about different things  and getting a random thoughts in the  middle of the night and when you're too  far from your phone or too far from a  notepad to write it down you can always  just say remind me to take out the trash  tonight at 6:00 p.m. or remind me to  pick up the washing from the laundry at  5:00 p.m. you can really tell it to do  anything and we're going straight to  your phone if you've set it up correctly  now talking about the setup of Google it  is very simple and quick to do and  there's a million tutorials on YouTube  so I won't do one of them but if you're  not tech savvy or if you are tech savvy  regardless of the fact it is very simple  to set up  you do need a smart phone though to make  it work and a good Wi-Fi connection so  make sure you have both of those before  you go out and buy one of these little  speakers the fourth reason why these  little speakers are great and I guess  it's something that Google is doing to  kind of encourage you to purchase more  and more of their products is the fact  that you can tell it to stream anything  to your TV or to a chromecast now we've  purchased a chromecast for our house  we've got it plugged into the TV so we  can always just go play something on  Netflix and it's gonna play whatever we  decide most of the time it's something  like I don't know the Fresh Prince of  bel-air  shoutout to Lou Smith but yeah the  Google Homes linked with the Google home  ultras  fantastic little things that you can  really link up and sync up and they're  great if you're sitting on your laptop  want to cast your screen to the TV I  don't know show some documents show some  different photos you can really share  the whole experience with the family  which is great if you don't have a smart  TV already now I'm going to break the  rules here and my fifth point of action  is actually going to be a negative one  in Australia at least so far in  Australia you can't make phone calls or  send text messages through the Google  home or the Google home Mini  unfortunately this is a feature that is  slowly being rolled out into the US but  it hasn't made it to Australia yet and  20  which is a bit of a chop ball but it  will eventually come through which I'm  looking forward to because telling  Google to quickly send a message to  anybody will be super convenient when  you're too far from your phone or busy  doing something potentially even you're  cutting chicken or making some food and  your hands are full so basically having  a remote speaker in your house which is  a phone accessory will be a great  addition to any household and make it a  budget smart home for under 50 bucks and  there you have it guys that's my review  of the Google home and the Google home  Mini if you enjoyed this video make sure  you smash that subscribe button  20:19 style I'm releasing a new video  every single Monday on different tech  and e-commerce advice so if you have an  interest in any of those things I'll see  you next Monday what's the weather like  currently 20 and clear on Saturday it'll  be mostly sunny with a high of 26 and a  low of 16

